ios-safari-debug-stack (0.2.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * CDP bridge: recover when Puppeteer hands back an execution-context id
    WebKit has already destroyed. Runtime.callFunctionOn resolves its
    receiver by evaluating `this` in the requested context; WebKit answers
    "missing injected script for given execution context id" once the realm
    is gone, which broke page.evaluate() after a page created or replaced a
    realm (observed live on a page starting an AudioWorklet). The receiver
    is now re-resolved against the page's current main world, and the error
    text reports WebKit's own message instead of "[object Object]".

 -- AppMana Engineering <engineering@appmana.com>  Wed, 16 Sep 2026 19:20:00 -0700

ios-safari-debug-stack (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * CDP bridge: detect and recover from a dead Web Inspector tunnel. The USB
    link to webinspectord can stop carrying traffic without closing, after
    which /json/list kept advertising pages from a Safari process that no
    longer existed and every command sent to them was silently dropped. Each
    source is now heartbeated with _rpc_getConnectedApplications:, declared
    dead after 12s of silence or on transport close, purged from the listing
    cache, and re-attached automatically by UDID.
  * CDP bridge: a target never silently drops a command. Every request now
    carries a 30s watchdog (INSPECT_WEBKIT_COMMAND_TIMEOUT_MS) that answers
    with an explicit protocol error naming the app and page, and sessions
    torn down by the server fail their in-flight commands and close the
    socket with a reason.
  * CDP bridge: implement Page.navigate for iOS 27, which removed it from
    WebKit's Page domain. The bridge probes once per session and otherwise
    drives the navigation from the page, reporting the frame and loader ids
    from the resulting Page.frameNavigated. Fixes puppeteer page.goto().
  * CDP bridge: stop mapping Emulation.setTouchEmulationEnabled onto
    Page.setTouchEmulationEnabled, removed in iOS 27. The failure made
    puppeteer.connect() and browser.pages() throw unless the caller passed
    defaultViewport: null.
  * CDP bridge: serve /json/version/ and /json/list/ with a trailing slash,
    so Playwright's chromium.connectOverCDP() discovery succeeds.
  * CDP bridge: answer Playwright's browser-level handshake —
    Target.getTargetInfo, Browser.setDownloadBehavior, permission and window
    stubs — and return explicit -32601 errors for Target.createTarget and the
    other tab-lifecycle methods WIR cannot provide, instead of dropping the
    browser socket.
  * CDP bridge: classify WIRTypeKey exactly. Service-worker and worker
    targets are no longer reported as type "page", are excluded from
    /json/list and from browser-level auto-attach, and unknown WIR types are
    reported as "other" rather than "page".
  * Tests: add an in-process fake Web Inspector device and end-to-end
    coverage for Puppeteer connect/pages/evaluate/goto, the Playwright
    handshake, trailing-slash discovery, wedged-target timeouts, tunnel loss
    and re-attach.

 -- AppMana Engineering <engineering@appmana.com>  Wed, 16 Sep 2026 18:30:00 -0700

